"DATA","SD04","SD","","258143.72","664789.09","","4.82","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 1.20m depth.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 31.50m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  5. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 31.50m to 39.00m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  6. 50mm diameter standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed to 8.00m depth on completion. Response zone 2.00m to 8.00m depth.","39.50","2019-05-20","","","2019-05-22","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""
"DATA","SD05","SD","","258191.45","664790.77","","4.82","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 1.20m depth.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Due to blowing sands no SPT test was carried out at 27.00m depth.  5. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 31.50m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  6. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 31.50m to 39.60m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  7. Dual standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed on completion. 19mm shallow installation installed to 2.00m, response zone 1.00m to 2.00m depth. 50mm deep installation installed to 9.00m, response zone 2.50m to 9.00m depth.","39.60","2019-05-23","","","2019-05-28","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""
"DATA","SD06","SD","","258339.46","664802.56","","4.85","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Ground surface broken out by hydraulic breaker. No inspection pit carried out due to concrete slab.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Due to blowing sands no SPT test was carried out between 16.50m to 19.50m and between 25.50m to 27.00m depth.  5. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 34.50m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  6. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 34.50m to 39.60m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  7. 50mm diameter standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed to 11.00m depth on completion. Response zone 1.00m to 11.00m depth.","39.50","2019-06-04","","","2019-06-06","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""
"DATA","SD07","SD","","257322.71","665055.72","","4.96","1. Borehole drilled by sonic drilling technique, in place of proposed window sample at this location, due to shallow ground obstructions.  2. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  3. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 0.20m depth.  4. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  5. Due to blowing sands no SPT testing was carried out at 13.50m, between 18.00m and 19.50m and at 28.50m depth.  6. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 31.50m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  7. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 31.50m to 36.50m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  8. Dual standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed on completion. 19mm shallow installation installed to 7.00m, response zone 1.00m to 7.00m depth. 50mm deep installation installed to 15.00m, response zone 8.00m to 15.00m depth.","36.50","2019-04-30","","","2019-05-03","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""
"DATA","SD08","SD","","257430.38","665024.15","","5.14","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 0.42m depth.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Due to blowing sands no SPT testing was carried out at between 18.00m and 19.50m depth.  5. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 31.50m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  6. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 31.50m to 36.50m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  7. 50mm diameter standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed to 7.30m depth on completion. Response zone 1.00m to 7.30m depth.","36.50","2019-04-24","","","2019-04-26","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","","",""
