"DATA","BHW01","0.00","15.00","CP","2019-04-23T00:00","2019-04-24T00:00","WWhitelaw","Dando 2000","","","","","","","","","CDavidson","","1. Down borehole checks for buried ferrous objects carried out during drilling by specialist unexploded ordnance (UXO) officer using magnetometer at regular intervals to 9.10m depth.  2. No groundwater strikes were recorded due to working overwater.  3. Borehole commenced using cable percussion drilling techniques at 203mm diameter down to 15.00m below sea bed level.  4. Rotary percussive ('open hole') methods between 15.00m to 16.40m, 17.90m to 19.00m, and 20.00m to 21.00m at 121mm diameter.  5. Rotary coring techniques from 21.00m to 28.00m using a PWF barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 87mm with liner.  6. Borehole backfilled with bentonite pellets and arisings upon completion.","","","",""
