"DATA","BHW05","0.00","20.10","CP","2019-05-03T00:00","2019-05-07T00:00","WWhitelaw","Dando 2000","","","","","","","","","CDavidson","","1. Down borehole checks for buried ferrous objects carried out during drilling by specialist unexploded ordnance (UXO) officer using magnetometer at regular intervals to 10.20m depth.  2. No groundwater strikes were recorded due to working over water.  3. Borehole commenced using cable percussion drilling techniques at 203mm diameter down to 20.10m below sea bed level.  4. Rotary percussive ('open hole') methods between 20.10m and 21.50m depth at 121mm diameter.  5. Rotary coring techniques from 20.10m to 26.70m using a PWF barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 87mm with liner.  6. Borehole backfilled with bentonite pellets and arisings upon completion.","","","",""
