"DATA","BHW09","0.00","19.00","CP","2019-05-22T00:00","2019-05-23T00:00","WWhitelaw","Dando 2000","","","","","","","","","CDavidson","","1. Down borehole checks for buried ferrous objects carried out during drilling by specialist unexploded ordnance (UXO) officer using magnetometer at regular intervals to 10.60m depth.  2. No groundwater strikes were recorded due to working over water.  3. Borehole commenced using cable percussion drilling techniques at 203mm diameter down to 19.00m below sea bed level.  4. Rotary percussive ('open hole') methods between 19.00m and 20.50m depth at 121mm diameter.  5. Rotary coring techniques from 20.50m to 26.30m using a PWF barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 87mm with liner.  6. Borehole backfilled with bentonite pellets and arisings upon completion.  7. Clay - like matrix described probably a product of the weathering of siltstone.","","","",""
