"DATA","SD01","0.00","10.50","SD","2019-04-29T00:00","2019-04-29T00:00","SWatt","DB320","","","","","","","","","ZCockburn","","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 1.20m depth.  3. Borehole drilled using sonic drilling techniques producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  4. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  5. 50mm diameter standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed to 4.50m depth on completion. Response zone 1.00m to 4.50m depth.","","","",""
"DATA","SD02","0.00","43.20","SD","2019-05-10T00:00","2019-05-15T00:00","SWatt","DB320","","","","","","","","","ZCockburn","2019-05-15","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 1.20m depth.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Due to blowing sands between 19.50m and 25.50m no SPT testing was carried out.  5. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 33.00m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  6. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 33.00m to 43.50m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  7. Dual standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed on completion. 19mm shallow installation installed to 4.50m, response zone 1.00m to 4.50m depth. 50mm deep installation installed to 11.00m, response zone 5.50m to 11.00m depth.","","","",""
"DATA","SD03","0.00","40.20","SD","2019-05-06T00:00","2019-05-09T00:00","SWatt","DB320","","","","","","","","","LBlair","2019-05-07","1. Position checked with Ground Penetrating Radar, CAT and Genny prior to excavation.  2. Hand excavated inspection pit from GL to 1.00m depth.  3. Could not determine any water strikes due to drilling with water.  4. Due to blowing sands no SPT testing was carried out at 18.00m depth or between 21.00m and 27.00m depth.  5. Borehole commenced using sonic drilling techniques to 35.00m producing a hole of 114mm diameter.  6. Borehole continued using coring techniques from 35.00m to 40.20m using a T2-101 barrel producing a nominal core diameter of 80.7mm with liner. Using water as flush medium.  7. Dual standpipe piezometer (complete with flush protective cover) installed on completion. 19mm shallow installation installed to 5.50m, response zone 1.00m to 5.50m depth. 50mm deep installation installed to 12.00m, response zone 6.50m to 12.00m depth.","","","",""
